# Testing and definition of done

Full matrix: `docs/testing/strategy.md`.

| Category | Covers |
|----------|--------|
| UNIT | parsers, normalization, correlation, sanitization, policy filters |
| INTEGRATION | PostgreSQL, migrations, persistence, history, tenant isolation, API, MCP |
| TRANSPORT | success, timeout, EOF, auth failure, malformed/partial output, custom port, read-only allowlist |
| COLLECTOR | complete / partial / failed / indeterminate; idempotent re-run |
| SECURITY | cross-tenant, command injection, secret redaction, unsafe command blocked |
| PERSISTENCE | DB restart, repeated ingest, temporal history, no artificial duplication |
| REAL LAB | optional, private credentials, **not** public CI, **never** Git fixtures |

Public tests run in Docker (`make test`). Lab targets (`lab-collect`, `lab-validate`) stay out of public CI.

A feature is not DONE because code exists. Proportional DoD:

- implementation + relevant tests
- migration if schema changed
- docs/contract updated
- tenant isolation checked
- errors sanitized
- real application path exercised (API/MCP, not SQL-only, when those are the consumers)
- no private data in the diff

Collectors: **IMPLEMENTATION** ≠ **TEST** ≠ **LAB VALIDATION** ≠ **OPERATIONAL VALIDATION**.
